  "content": {
    "title": "Here's when 'Euphoria' season 3 comes out and how to watch the series",
    "text": "April 11, 2026, 4:27 p.m. ETAfter more than four years of anticipation, season 3 of the hit show \"Euphoria\" will finally be released this weekend.The latest installment of HBO's Emmy-winning series comes after the show reportedly faced several production delays, including the 2023 Hollywood actor and screenwriter strikes.\"Euphoria\" became a TV darling and pop culture lightning rod thanks to its frank take on adolescent life, including its graphic portrayals of sexuality and drug use.Here is everything you need to know about the show's upcoming, and possibly final, season:When does season 3 of 'Euphoria' come out?Season 3 of \"Euphoria\" comes out on Sunday, April 12, at 9 p.m. Eastern time. The season will feature eight one-hour episodes, releasing at the same time every Sunday.Where can I watch 'Euphoria'?Season 3 of \"Euphoria\" will stream on HBO Max, with season 1 and 2 of the show currently available on the platform.A subscription is required to stream the show. Subscription plans range from $10.99 to $22.99 per month.What is 'Euphoria' about?The first two seasons of \"Euphoria\" explore the troubled lives of high school students, featuring themes of addiction, sexuality and mental illness. Season 3 takes place five years later, following the characters as they navigate adulthood. Zendaya's Rue works as an indentured servant for drug dealer Laurie (Martha Kelly), while Cassie (Sydney Sweeney) and Nate (Jacob Elordi) navigate married life.This article includes reporting from USA Today.",
